WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.800
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:11.840
Today we are going to see magical things that&nbsp;
open up when we are able to automatically find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.960
the foreground and the background of a video.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.440
Let’s see why that matters!

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:24.880
This new technique leans on a previous method&nbsp;
to find the boy, and the dog. Let’s call this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:31.600
level 1 segmentation. So far so good, but&nbsp;
this is not the state of the art. Yet.&nbsp;

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:38.880
Now, comes level 2 - it also found the shadow&nbsp;
of the boy, and, the shadow of the dog.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.120
Now we’re talking!
But it doesn’t stop there!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:49.520
It gets even better. Level three, this&nbsp;
is where things get out of hand - look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.640
the dog is occluding the boy’s shadow,&nbsp;
and it is able to deal with that too.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:02.080
So, if we can identify all of the effects that&nbsp;
are attached to the boy and the dog, what can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:08.560
we do with all this information? Well, for&nbsp;
instance, we can even remove them from the video.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:15.680
Nothing to see here. Now, a common problem&nbsp;
is that still, the silhouette of the subject&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.480
still remains in the final footage,&nbsp;
so let’s take a close look together!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.840
I don’t see anything at all. Wow. Do&nbsp;
you? Let me know in the comments below!

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:35.120
Just to showcase how good this removal is, here&nbsp;
is a good technique from just one year ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.040
Do you see it? This requires the&nbsp;
shadows to be found manually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:47.360
so we have to work with that. And still, in the&nbsp;
outputs, you can see the silhouette we mentioned.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:55.920
And, how much better is the new method?&nbsp;
Well, it finds the shadows automatically.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:04.640
That is already mind blowing, and the outputs&nbsp;
are…yes, much cleaner. Not perfect, there is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.240
some silhouette action, but if I were not actively&nbsp;
looking for it, I might not have noticed it.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.880
It can also remove people&nbsp;
from this trampoline scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:23.120
and not only the bodies, but it also removes&nbsp;
their effect on the trampolines as well. Wow.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.320
And as this method can perform&nbsp;
all this reliably, it opens up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:34.640
the possibility for new, magical effects.
For instance, we can duplicate this test subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:42.400
and even fade it in and out. Note that it&nbsp;
has found its shadows as well. Excellent!

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:48.000
So, it can deal with finding not only&nbsp;
the shape of the boy and the dog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.160
and it knows that it’s not enough to just find&nbsp;
their silhouettes, but it also has to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:03:01.120
additional effects they have on the footage.&nbsp;
For instance, their shadows. That is wonderful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.480
and what is even more wonderful is that this&nbsp;
was only one of the simpler things it could do.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.800
Shadows are not the only&nbsp;
potential correlated effects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:16.400
look. A previous method was able to find the&nbsp;
swan here, but that’s not enough to remove it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:24.640
because it has additional effects on the scene.&nbsp;
What are those? Well, look, it has reflections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:32.240
and it creates ripples too. This is so much&nbsp;
more difficult than just finding shadows.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:39.920
And now, let’s see the new method..and! Whoa.&nbsp;
It knows about the reflections and ripples,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:46.720
finds both of them, and gives us this&nbsp;
beautifully clean result. Nothing to see here.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.360
Also, look at this elephant. Removing&nbsp;
just the silhouette of the elephant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:57.200
is not enough, it also has to&nbsp;
find all the dust around it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:04.320
and it gets worse, the dust is changing&nbsp;
rapidly over time. And believe it or not…wow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:12.800
it can find the dust too, and remove the&nbsp;
elephant. Again, nothing to see here.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:19.280
And if you think that this dust was the new&nbsp;
algorithm at its best, then have a look at this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:28.400
drifting car. Previous method. Yes, that is the&nbsp;
car, but you know what I want. I want the smoke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:39.360
gone too. That’s probably impossible, right?&nbsp;
Well, let’s have a look. Wow. I can’t believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:46.480
it. It grabbed and removed the car and the smoke&nbsp;
together…and, once again, nothing to see here.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:52.640
So, what are those more magical things&nbsp;
that this opens up? Watch carefully…it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.280 --> 00:05:01.280
can make the colors pop here. And, remember, it&nbsp;
can find the reflections of the flamingo, so, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:10.320
keeps not only the flamingo, but the reflection of&nbsp;
the flamingo in color as well. Absolutely amazing.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:16.960
And, if we can find the background of a video,&nbsp;
we can even change the background. This works&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.960
even in the presence of a moving&nbsp;
camera, which is a challenging problem.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:28.320
Now, of course, not even this technique is&nbsp;
perfect - look here. The reflections are copied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.760
off of the previous scene,&nbsp;
and it shows on the new one.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.960
So what do you think? What would&nbsp;
you use this technique for?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:42.080
Let me know in the comments, or if you wish&nbsp;
to discuss similar topics with other Fellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:48.160
Scholars in a warm and welcoming environment,&nbsp;
make sure to join our Discord channel. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

